sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body faithfully reproduces African leopard (Panthera pardus) coat rosettes and tapered tail markings morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) 1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real African leopard (Panthera pardus) coat rosettes and tapered tail markings specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 84.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-mammalian-coat-markings-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py; output: docs/media/mammalian_coat_markings_comparison.png; organism: African leopard (Panthera pardus) coat rosettes and tapered tail markings; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/64526a0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: b990576b2a4b3ccd36c08d1a21625f5ebd87766fc673675eaee0d8216821ffd3; artifact_sha256: 417dee8b24b004962c52143eefd329402da37f468ef4c9cbd844a2d13282558a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/felid_body_profile.json=65978462afc1b9e7..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/mammalian_coat_markings_reference.json=24d56069831e0ee9..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/panthera_pardus_specimen.jpg=86533a5dcf9cfee6..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/scout_manifest.json=28eabc9cf247b03e...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-mammalian-coat-markings-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Murray (1981): Thomas substrate-inhibition kinetics at a = 92, b = 64, alpha = 1.5, rho = 18.5, K = 0.1 are diffusively unstable for d > d_c; the domain scale factor gamma selects between no pattern, stripes, spots and crowding; on a tapered cylinder spot modes (m >= 1) are excluded below a critical radius so a spotted animal can have a ringed tail but not vice versa | Liu, Liaw & Maini (2006): leopard rosettes arise from a two-stage process in which a juvenile spot pre-pattern is re-run under changed parameters on the grown adult skin | Dziuk (1988), Pinkall & Polthier (1993), Dziuk & Elliott (2013): P1 surface finite elements with cotangent weights converge to the Laplace-Beltrami operator on a triangulated surface; reconstructed_in_script: Exact steady state, Jacobian, d_c, dispersion curve and Turing band; Neumann cylinder eigenmode counting including n = 0; r_crit (fastest-mode) and r_excl = 1/k_+ (full-exclusion) radii; fully implicit conical-tail PDE; planar DCT-II IMEX PDE run to saturation with a genuine two-stage protocol and growth-factor sweep; P1 surface FEM (stiffness/mass assembly, spectrum verification, two-stage run on the felid body) with annularity and spot-spacing diagnostics; DoG segmentation of the Kruger specimen; transfer_boundary: The 3D body is a parametric surface of revolution with hand-set knots (felid_body_profile.json), not a photogrammetric scan; its head-body length of 22 cub wavelengths and the growth factor G = 2 are ASSUMED, not fitted, which is why the FEM marking density (5.1 per torso depth) is 3.7x below the specimen estimate (18.9) | The tail ring onset comparison (0.82 measured vs 0.86 predicted) is on the surrogate taper, whose tip radius (0.004 HBL) was chosen to lie below r_excl; it is a consistency check of solver against linear theory, not a measurement on a real tail | The specimen is a 3/4-view photograph: the flank ROI is foreshortened and the v2 tail ROI covers hindquarters/background, so the Delaunay CV and polygonality are flank-only statistics; does_not_claim: That Murray (1981) or Liu et al. (2006) reported any of the FEM, annularity, growth-sweep or marking-density numbers; all are v3 reconstructions | That the Thomas kinetics are the biological mechanism of felid pigmentation]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0082865>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0300-9084(75)80312-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0962492913000056>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/scientificamerican0388-80>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1080/10586458.1993.10504266>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.74.011914>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1644/900.1> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.842"^^xsd:double .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "64526a0" .
}

